WEBVTT

00:03.215 --> 00:06.183
Oh, my God. Oh, my God!
(moaning): Oh... oh, my God.

00:06.185 --> 00:09.019
Oh... Oh, my God, Jenny!
Oh, my God.

00:09.021 --> 00:10.420
Yeah. Oh...
Oh, my God.

00:10.422 --> 00:13.023
Oh, my &lt;i>God.&lt;/i>

00:13.025 --> 00:15.259
Oh, Jenny!
Give it to me.

00:15.261 --> 00:16.793
Give it to me,
Jenny.

00:16.795 --> 00:18.829
Just give it to her
already.

00:18.831 --> 00:22.432
(women continue
exclaiming, moaning)

00:24.869 --> 00:25.769
Hey.

00:25.771 --> 00:27.404
Hey. Couldn't sleep, either?

00:27.406 --> 00:30.474
No. Jenny and her friend
are crazy in there.

00:30.476 --> 00:33.277
Have you ever made
a woman scream like that?

00:33.279 --> 00:34.344
Once.

00:34.346 --> 00:36.213
I hit her with my car.

00:36.215 --> 00:37.881
It sounded like Jenny hit her

00:37.883 --> 00:41.151
and then backed over her again.

00:41.153 --> 00:42.786
And then hit her,

00:42.788 --> 00:45.155
a-and then...
backed over her again.

00:46.591 --> 00:48.525
And then hit her...

00:48.527 --> 00:50.360
and then backed over her again.

00:50.362 --> 00:53.630
I counted eight orgasms,
not including mine.

00:53.632 --> 00:54.998
Hey, that's my niece.
Oh, yeah,

00:55.000 --> 00:57.968
and out of respect to you,
I only listened to her friend.

00:57.970 --> 01:00.103
Yeah, me, too.

01:01.172 --> 01:03.307
Hey, how about
this weekend &lt;i>we&lt;/i> go out

01:03.309 --> 01:05.475
and find some women
and make 'em scream?

01:06.344 --> 01:08.178
In-in your imagination,

01:08.180 --> 01:11.415
are they running away from you
or towards you?

01:11.417 --> 01:12.983
You know what I mean.

01:12.985 --> 01:15.185
Let's go out
and find some &lt;i>strange.&lt;/i>

01:15.187 --> 01:18.388
I'm looking at some &lt;i>strange.&lt;/i>

01:18.390 --> 01:20.290
Besides, I can't.

01:20.292 --> 01:22.159
My mom's got a charity dinner
this weekend.

01:22.161 --> 01:24.027
Oh, she's still trying
to help the monkeys?

01:24.029 --> 01:27.264
Yeah, she's raising money
to expand her sanctuary

01:27.266 --> 01:30.400
for helpless creatures
that nobody else wants.

01:30.402 --> 01:32.102
Kind of like what I do for you.

01:32.104 --> 01:34.605
Will there be any
single ladies there

01:34.607 --> 01:36.506
looking to use those
opposable thumbs?

01:36.508 --> 01:39.343
You know, swing on my vine,
peel my banana.

01:39.345 --> 01:41.011
Well, there might be a few there

01:41.013 --> 01:43.213
that want to throw
their poop at you.

01:43.215 --> 01:45.782
Mm, sounds like a good cause;
I'll buy a ticket.

01:45.784 --> 01:48.752
They're a thousand
dollars apiece.

01:48.754 --> 01:51.955
Can I borrow $998?

01:51.957 --> 01:53.156
Hey.

01:53.158 --> 01:55.058
Hey.
Hey.

01:58.196 --> 01:59.596
(whirring)

01:59.598 --> 02:01.031
That'll work.

02:01.866 --> 02:03.233
You know what they say:

02:03.235 --> 02:07.137
once you go Black &amp; Decker,
you never go back.

02:07.139 --> 02:09.706
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

02:09.708 --> 02:12.409
♪ Ah.
♪ Men.

02:12.434 --> 02:16.434
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 11x06 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Justice in Star-Spangled Hot Pants&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on November 7, 2013

02:16.459 --> 02:21.459
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

02:24.194 --> 02:26.095
Hey! Look at you.

02:26.097 --> 02:28.097
Where are you going
in that monkey suit?

02:28.099 --> 02:29.799
A benefit.

02:29.801 --> 02:31.834
For monkeys.

02:33.136 --> 02:34.737
How do I look?

02:34.739 --> 02:37.073
Like you should be
on top of a cake.

02:37.075 --> 02:38.941
Let me guess: you're the cake.

02:38.943 --> 02:43.612
No, I'm the one that gets
to blow out the candle.

02:46.249 --> 02:49.552
Oh, when did we install
a mirror in here?

02:49.554 --> 02:51.087
(chuckles)
Tell the truth, Berta,

02:51.089 --> 02:52.822
you ever seen
two better-looking guys?

02:52.824 --> 02:54.223
No.

02:54.225 --> 02:55.691
Yes.

02:56.960 --> 03:00.229
(doorbell rings)
Oh. That must be my date.

03:02.032 --> 03:04.367
Hi, honey.
(laughs) You look amazing.

03:04.369 --> 03:07.003
Oh, you look so handsome.

03:07.005 --> 03:08.537
Wow, nice job, Walden.

03:08.539 --> 03:09.972
Where'd you two meet?

03:09.974 --> 03:12.074
Kind of a "meet cute."

03:12.076 --> 03:13.743
I shot out of her.

03:13.745 --> 03:15.578
Jenny, this is
my mom, Robin.

03:15.580 --> 03:18.247
Mom, this is my new
roommate, Jenny.

03:18.249 --> 03:19.915
Oh, well, it's
a pleasure to meet you.

03:19.917 --> 03:21.517
(gasps)
Alan,

03:21.519 --> 03:23.085
does this mean
you finally moved out?

03:23.087 --> 03:25.054
(hearty laughter)

03:26.223 --> 03:27.823
No, no, no,
Jenny's my niece.

03:27.825 --> 03:29.191
She's staying
in Jake's room.

03:29.193 --> 03:32.461
Well, I have my charity,
you have yours.

03:33.430 --> 03:35.931
I can see where Walden
gets his pretty face.

03:35.933 --> 03:37.266
Aren't you sweet?

03:37.268 --> 03:38.501
He's single, you know.

03:38.503 --> 03:40.736
I know. Are you?

03:42.305 --> 03:44.206
Okay. All right, let's...

03:44.208 --> 03:47.276
go save some monkeys.

03:47.278 --> 03:48.978
(clears throat softly)

03:48.980 --> 03:50.413
Really?

03:50.415 --> 03:51.947
Hey, just 'cause
you came out of it

03:51.949 --> 03:54.550
doesn't mean
I don't want to get into it.

03:58.422 --> 04:01.090
(scoffs) They call
these martinis?

04:01.092 --> 04:04.026
The only thing they're saving
the monkeys from are DUI's.

04:04.028 --> 04:05.394
(laughing)

04:05.396 --> 04:06.829
You like that one?

04:06.831 --> 04:11.133
No, I was just picturing
a drunk monkey driving a car.

04:12.302 --> 04:14.103
Walden.
Mm.

04:14.105 --> 04:15.404
Oh.

04:15.406 --> 04:17.973
That woman with your mom
looks just like Lynda Carter.

04:17.975 --> 04:20.443
(Alan laughs)

04:20.445 --> 04:21.744
That is Lynda Carter.

04:21.746 --> 04:22.978
Really?

04:22.980 --> 04:24.947
Wait, wait, T-TV's
Wonder Woman?

04:24.949 --> 04:26.482
The jewel of
Paradise Island?

04:26.484 --> 04:30.019
The-the shining crusader for justice
and star-spangled hot pants?

04:30.021 --> 04:32.321
I-I just call her Lynda.

04:32.323 --> 04:35.691
And I just lost the cleaning
deposit on this tux.

04:35.693 --> 04:36.892
Walden.

04:36.894 --> 04:38.761
Lynda, you look amazing.

04:38.763 --> 04:41.464
Oh, my God.
The last time we saw each other,

04:41.466 --> 04:43.165
you barely came up to here.

04:43.167 --> 04:45.835
I remember those... days.

04:46.603 --> 04:48.804
(clearing throat):
Introduce me.

04:48.806 --> 04:51.073
Robin, you told me
he was successful,

04:51.075 --> 04:53.509
but you didn't tell me
how gorgeous he is.

04:53.511 --> 04:56.011
Well, it takes
a gorgeous person to know one.

04:56.013 --> 04:57.346
(laughs)

04:57.348 --> 04:59.615
(nervous laughing):
No, it doesn't. I'm Alan.

04:59.617 --> 05:01.417
Hi.

05:01.419 --> 05:04.443
This is Alan Harper.
He lives with Walden.

05:04.468 --> 05:05.188
Oh, well, it's lovely

05:05.189 --> 05:06.355
to meet you.

05:06.357 --> 05:09.258
My gay fans have always been
my biggest supporters.

05:09.260 --> 05:11.527
Oh, oh, no, no, I-I'm not gay.

05:11.529 --> 05:14.230
Oh, I'm sorry.
Transgender?

05:15.132 --> 05:17.066
I told you the hormones
weren't working.

05:17.068 --> 05:18.200
(chuckles)

05:18.202 --> 05:20.336
He's kidding.
Uh, I-I am very straight.

05:20.338 --> 05:23.706
In fact, the longer I look
at you the straighter I become.

05:23.708 --> 05:26.575
Well, if you'll excuse us,
I'm gonna start a fund

05:26.577 --> 05:29.512
to, um, save Lynda
from this conversation.

05:29.514 --> 05:31.680
(giggles)
It's lovely to meet you.

05:31.682 --> 05:34.984
And it was "wonder-ful"
meeting you. (chuckles)

05:34.986 --> 05:37.720
That's funny. I've never
heard &lt;i>that&lt;/i> one before.

05:37.722 --> 05:39.421
Don't be a stranger.
Okay.

05:40.290 --> 05:41.924
Call me.
(chuckles)

05:44.461 --> 05:47.363
What the hell are you doing?

05:47.365 --> 05:51.000
Sorry, I just wanted to put
my mouth where her mouth was.

05:51.002 --> 05:53.502
And I also wanted to thank
you for a lovely evening.

05:58.308 --> 05:59.441
Morning.

05:59.443 --> 06:01.010
Mm. I got to tell you,

06:01.012 --> 06:03.913
you gave me a night
that I will never forget.

06:05.782 --> 06:08.617
Don't ever say that to me again.

06:08.619 --> 06:09.818
I'm serious.
Meeting Lynda Carter was

06:09.820 --> 06:11.587
one of the greatest moments
of my life.

06:11.589 --> 06:13.289
I mean, she was
my first celebrity crush.

06:13.291 --> 06:15.324
I had a poster of her
that looked like

06:15.326 --> 06:18.060
the bottom of a birdcage.

06:18.062 --> 06:22.431
On behalf of Lynda Carter
and the rest of humanity...

06:22.433 --> 06:24.233
yuck.

06:24.235 --> 06:26.802
You know, it's not just about
how beautiful she was.

06:26.804 --> 06:29.371
I mean, she's multitalented.
I mean, I had all of her albums,

06:29.373 --> 06:31.473
I-I-I've seen everything
she's ever done.

06:31.475 --> 06:32.875
How?

06:32.877 --> 06:35.444
Were you hiding outside
her house in a bush?

06:35.446 --> 06:37.646
(snorting laugh)

06:39.182 --> 06:42.251
Lynda Carter's bush.

06:44.087 --> 06:46.222
Hey, you know, she's single.

06:46.224 --> 06:47.456
And?

06:47.458 --> 06:49.191
And? (laughs)

06:49.193 --> 06:51.026
Set me up with her.

06:51.028 --> 06:54.463
Can't I just... get
you a new poster?

06:55.832 --> 06:57.833
I'll laminate it.

06:57.835 --> 06:59.935
Come on, come on.

06:59.937 --> 07:02.338
I-I-I have been in love with
Lynda Carter for my whole life,

07:02.340 --> 07:05.174
and because you know her
and I know you,

07:05.176 --> 07:06.875
I actually have a shot.

07:06.877 --> 07:08.310
I mean, this is fate.

07:08.312 --> 07:10.012
This is probably
why my brother died.

07:10.014 --> 07:12.481
You said fate
killed your brother

07:12.483 --> 07:14.617
so you could get
that espresso machine.

07:14.619 --> 07:16.352
Come on!

07:16.354 --> 07:17.953
I'll see what I can do.

07:17.955 --> 07:19.154
Really?

07:19.156 --> 07:20.723
Yeah. Just don't
get your hopes up.

07:20.725 --> 07:22.224
(scoffs):
Oh, of course not.

07:22.226 --> 07:23.826
Thank you.

07:25.228 --> 07:28.130
(quietly): Ladies and gentlemen, please
welcome to the dance floor,

07:28.132 --> 07:31.033
for the first time
as man and wife...

07:31.035 --> 07:34.003
Mr. and Mrs. Lynda Carter.

07:40.543 --> 07:43.045
Okay, great.
All right, we'll see you soon.

07:43.880 --> 07:45.347
Hey.

07:46.182 --> 07:47.549
Was that her?

07:47.551 --> 07:48.717
Who?

07:48.719 --> 07:51.487
(high-pitched):
♪ Wonder Woman!

07:52.522 --> 07:55.724
♪ For your friend,
Alan Harper! ♪

07:55.726 --> 07:56.992
What are you doing?

07:56.994 --> 07:59.028
Oh, it's the &lt;i>Wonder Woman&lt;/i>
theme song.

07:59.030 --> 08:00.963
(high-pitched):
♪ Wonder Woman!

08:00.965 --> 08:04.533
♪ You're a wonder,
Wonder Woman! ♪

08:04.535 --> 08:05.901
Not familiar.

08:05.903 --> 08:07.102
You should be, 'cause it's...

08:07.104 --> 08:09.605
♪ Kind of awesome!

08:09.607 --> 08:11.807
I was ordering a pizza.

08:12.776 --> 08:14.910
I haven't had a chance
to talk to her yet.

08:14.912 --> 08:16.378
Why not?

08:16.380 --> 08:19.081
♪ Does your word mean nothin'? ♪

08:19.083 --> 08:22.017
You know what, uh,
to be perfectly honest, I...

08:22.019 --> 08:24.653
I don't know
if this is a good idea.

08:24.655 --> 08:25.888
What? Why?

08:25.890 --> 08:27.656
What-what's wrong with her?
Is she crazy?

08:27.658 --> 08:30.359
I like crazy. You met Lyndsey--
that bitch is cuckoo.

08:30.361 --> 08:34.096
No, there's-there's
nothing wrong with her.

08:34.098 --> 08:35.230
So what's the problem?

08:35.232 --> 08:37.566
She's... Lynda Carter.

08:37.568 --> 08:39.601
And?

08:39.603 --> 08:41.804
And you're...

08:41.806 --> 08:44.840
(high-pitched):
♪ Alan Harper!

08:46.743 --> 08:48.510
Oh.

08:48.512 --> 08:50.379
Oh, I get it.

08:50.381 --> 08:52.748
You don't think
I'm good enough for her.

08:52.750 --> 08:54.583
Oh, no, it's not that.

08:54.585 --> 08:56.018
No, no, no, no, no,
it's fine, it's fine.

08:56.020 --> 08:58.420
Just out of curiosity,
who &lt;i>am&lt;/i> I good enough for?

08:58.422 --> 09:00.155
Lots of people.
Well, name one.

09:00.157 --> 09:01.857
Okay, how about...
how about the-the...

09:01.859 --> 09:03.892
the barista at the coffee place.

09:03.894 --> 09:06.195
The hot blonde, Vanessa?
Oh, God, no. No, I'm...

09:06.197 --> 09:07.796
I'm...

09:07.798 --> 09:09.064
I'm talking about the other one.

09:09.066 --> 09:11.333
The only other one is Miguel.

09:11.335 --> 09:14.937
No. No, Tracy.
The one with the brown hair.

09:14.939 --> 09:18.073
Coming out of her chin mole.

09:18.075 --> 09:19.575
Okay, then Miguel.

09:19.577 --> 09:22.644
(scoffs) I... I can't believe
you think so little of me.

09:22.646 --> 09:24.580
It's not that.
Oh, you know what? You know what?

09:24.582 --> 09:26.682
This is actually good.
I finally know where I stand

09:26.684 --> 09:27.716
with my "friend."

09:27.718 --> 09:28.851
Okay, Alan...

09:28.853 --> 09:31.687
And you were gonna
be our best man!

09:34.357 --> 09:37.025
Yeah, no, he's
not good enough for Miguel.

09:37.027 --> 09:38.527
♪ Men.

09:46.220 --> 09:47.953
(Jenny clears throat)

09:47.955 --> 09:49.322
Hey.

09:49.324 --> 09:51.023
Hey. You're up early.

09:51.025 --> 09:53.826
(sighs):
Yup. Crack of dawn.

09:53.828 --> 09:56.629
But, shh,
Dawn is still sleeping.

09:57.964 --> 09:59.332
Good morning.

09:59.334 --> 10:00.399
Good morning.

10:00.401 --> 10:02.435
Uh, hey, Jenny,
do you have any idea

10:02.437 --> 10:05.604
how to get tear stains
out of pillows?

10:05.606 --> 10:07.873
It's certainly not more tears,
because I tried that.

10:07.875 --> 10:09.141
Have you tried spraying

10:09.143 --> 10:11.344
some desperate
cry for attention on it?

10:13.347 --> 10:14.847
You want
some coffee?

10:14.849 --> 10:17.049
Why, yes, I would.
Oh, uh, Walden,

10:17.051 --> 10:18.751
is there some
uglier coffee

10:18.753 --> 10:20.553
that might be more
appropriate for me?

10:20.555 --> 10:22.688
All right.
Alan, you're being ridiculous.

10:22.690 --> 10:24.490
Hey, sticks and stones
may break my bones,

10:24.492 --> 10:26.992
but thanks to you,
I'll never bone Lynda Carter.

10:28.595 --> 10:32.231
Now, if you'll excuse me, I
will breakfast alone in my room.

10:32.233 --> 10:34.700
What's wrong with Auntie Alan?

10:34.702 --> 10:37.670
She's pouting 'cause I won't
set her up with Lynda Carter.

10:37.672 --> 10:40.940
Why not?
Because, it's Lynda Carter.

10:40.942 --> 10:42.775
Right.

10:42.777 --> 10:44.910
And who's Lynda Carter?

10:44.912 --> 10:47.179
Lynda Carter is an actress.

10:47.181 --> 10:49.949
Oh. And she makes you
say her whole name?

10:49.951 --> 10:51.417
She doesn't make you,

10:51.419 --> 10:54.086
it's just something you do
when people reach icon status.

10:54.088 --> 10:56.622
So why won't you
set Alan up with her?

10:56.624 --> 10:58.090
She's out of his league.

10:58.092 --> 10:59.291
What league is she in?

10:59.293 --> 11:02.595
Well, among others,
the Justice League.

11:02.597 --> 11:05.197
All right, I have no idea
what you're talking about,

11:05.199 --> 11:07.333
so let me just
ask you a question.

11:07.335 --> 11:08.948
Is Alan good enough
to be your friend?

11:08.973 --> 11:10.737
Of course.

11:10.738 --> 11:13.806
So then why isn't he good enough for her?
Okay, that's not fair.

11:13.808 --> 11:16.709
There are a lot of women that
Alan is not good enough for.

11:16.711 --> 11:20.279
Don't you think she should
decide who she can go out with?

11:20.281 --> 11:22.456
Hmm. That's actually
a good point.

11:22.457 --> 11:24.041
Hang on, one second,
is this Lynda Carter?

11:24.066 --> 11:25.852
Uh-huh.

11:25.853 --> 11:29.054
Yeah, Alan's not
good enough for her.

11:32.325 --> 11:34.026
(sighs)

11:34.028 --> 11:35.261
Alan.

11:35.263 --> 11:36.529
ALAN: Yeah?

11:36.531 --> 11:38.330
Are you decent?

11:38.332 --> 11:41.333
Not by your standards.

11:41.335 --> 11:43.836
Okay, I'm coming in.

11:43.838 --> 11:45.671
What do you want?

11:45.673 --> 11:48.474
If it's self-esteem you're
after, there's none here.

11:48.476 --> 11:50.443
I was wrong.

11:50.445 --> 11:54.146
It is not my place to decide
who you can or cannot date.

11:54.148 --> 11:55.147
No, no, it's fine.

11:55.149 --> 11:56.515
Uh, actually, I'm making a list

11:56.517 --> 11:58.017
of the people
you shouldn't date.

11:58.019 --> 12:01.454
Uh, Number one:
Anyone with a heart.

12:01.456 --> 12:03.422
Okay, you know, I deserve that.

12:03.424 --> 12:05.858
And number two,
Taylor Swift, because she will

12:05.860 --> 12:09.628
write a song about you called
"Back-Stabbing Dream Killer."

12:09.630 --> 12:11.430
Okay, well, if you will let me,

12:11.432 --> 12:13.999
I would like
to make it up to you.

12:14.001 --> 12:18.771
I invited my mother and Lynda
over for dinner tomorrow night.

12:18.773 --> 12:21.841
So, you are free
to ask her out yourself.

12:21.843 --> 12:24.176
If you're joking,
I swear to God

12:24.178 --> 12:27.079
I will pack my things and you
will never see me again.

12:27.081 --> 12:28.581
I was joking.
So was I.

12:28.583 --> 12:31.417
You're not just doing this
out of pity, are you?

12:31.419 --> 12:33.352
Don't answer, I don't care.

12:33.354 --> 12:34.353
You're a good friend.

12:34.355 --> 12:36.222
So are you.

12:36.224 --> 12:38.491
And, again, I'm sorry.

12:38.493 --> 12:40.092
Thank you.

12:40.094 --> 12:43.662
Okay. Oh, and,
and, a little tip:

12:43.664 --> 12:47.333
when Lynda's here, just try
not to act like a crazy fan.

12:47.335 --> 12:48.398
(chuckles) I got it.

12:48.423 --> 12:50.624
No, no, seriously, like, if,
if you want a shot with her

12:50.771 --> 12:53.005
you need to treat
her like she's a normal person.

12:53.007 --> 12:55.641
And, and you should
pretend to be one, yourself.

12:55.643 --> 12:57.409
It's not a problem.
(laughs)

13:00.947 --> 13:04.183
Until tomorrow.

13:06.820 --> 13:08.954
All right,
I'm out of here.

13:08.956 --> 13:11.590
Dinner's in the oven
and the wine's chilling.

13:11.592 --> 13:12.558
Oh, thank you.

13:12.560 --> 13:14.460
No, I was talking about
at my house.

13:14.462 --> 13:17.663
Oh, oh, uh, uh,
before you go, um,

13:17.665 --> 13:20.065
uh, uh, which is my good side?
What?

13:20.067 --> 13:22.034
I'm trying to figure out
where to sit at dinner.

13:22.036 --> 13:24.036
I-I want my good side
facing Lynda.

13:24.038 --> 13:25.571
All right.

13:25.573 --> 13:27.172
Turn to your left.

13:27.174 --> 13:28.274
Okay.

13:28.276 --> 13:29.508
Now turn to your right.

13:29.510 --> 13:31.310
Okay.

13:31.312 --> 13:33.646
Turn around.

13:33.648 --> 13:37.449
Perfect.

13:37.451 --> 13:39.652
Who hurt you, Berta?

13:39.654 --> 13:41.153
(doorbell rings)

13:41.155 --> 13:42.721
Oh, uh...

13:45.725 --> 13:48.227
Ooh, uh, just in case.

13:51.431 --> 13:53.332
Oh, God, it burns!

13:55.602 --> 13:58.470
What did I say about
acting like a normal person?

13:58.472 --> 14:02.541
That was before I got mint spray
in Little Alan's eye.

14:02.543 --> 14:04.677
I'm not even gonna ask.

14:06.112 --> 14:08.714
Oh, hey, you two
look beautiful.

14:08.716 --> 14:11.050
Oh, it's great
to see you again, Walden.

14:11.052 --> 14:12.751
And don't forget about me.
(chuckles)

14:12.753 --> 14:16.121
Oh, don't worry, I haven't.

14:16.123 --> 14:19.692
Okay, you can let go now.

14:19.694 --> 14:21.694
Well, I'm glad
you two could make it.

14:21.696 --> 14:24.597
Wow, this is quite the place.

14:24.599 --> 14:26.799
BOTH:
Thank you.

14:26.801 --> 14:28.567
Single guy living at the beach,

14:28.569 --> 14:30.603
you must do well
with the ladies.

14:30.605 --> 14:34.974
I do okay, but this guy
is the real charmer.

14:34.976 --> 14:39.945
Blink twice if you're
being held against your will.

14:39.947 --> 14:41.280
Well, it's,
it's true, in my youth

14:41.282 --> 14:43.482
I was a bit of a,
a rapscallion.

14:43.484 --> 14:44.817
(nervous chuckle)

14:44.819 --> 14:46.051
A rake.

14:46.053 --> 14:48.087
A... gadabout.

14:48.089 --> 14:50.556
WALDEN:
A... g-gadabout?

14:50.558 --> 14:52.391
What have you.

14:52.393 --> 14:55.227
Yeah, but that was
in your past, right?

14:55.229 --> 14:58.364
And now you're just a
normal, regular guy?

14:58.366 --> 14:59.465
Yeah, that's right,
that's right.

14:59.467 --> 15:02.568
I'm just a,
a normal, regular guy

15:02.570 --> 15:06.138
looking for a crazy
little thing called love.

15:06.140 --> 15:09.775
LYNDA CARTER:
♪ Crazy little thing called love... ♪

15:09.777 --> 15:12.845
What's that I hear?

15:12.847 --> 15:17.149
Is that the lovely voice of
triple-threat Lynda Carter?

15:17.151 --> 15:20.452
Actress, singer, dancer?

15:20.454 --> 15:23.455
Wait a second,
do I smell mint?

15:26.459 --> 15:30.129
Yes, and it's not
coming from my mouth.

15:35.402 --> 15:37.169
Oh ,uh, uh,
would you mind signing it

15:37.171 --> 15:40.305
"From a Wonder Woman
to a Super Man"?

15:42.509 --> 15:45.377
How about "best wishes"?
That works. (chuckles)

15:45.379 --> 15:46.945
Hey, you know,
I'll, I'll bet you could

15:46.947 --> 15:48.347
make a lot of money
traveling around

15:48.349 --> 15:49.882
and signing
at conventions and stuff.

15:49.884 --> 15:51.850
I'm not a big fan of travel.

15:51.852 --> 15:54.219
Yeah, not to mention
the weirdos you'd meet.

15:54.221 --> 15:56.455
Ugh. You don't
have to tell me,

15:56.457 --> 15:58.490
I mean, I-I've talked
to a lot of them

15:58.492 --> 16:02.261
on the Wonder Woman
message boards. Freaks!

16:03.430 --> 16:05.130
Alan?
Hmm?

16:05.132 --> 16:06.965
I'm pretty sure Lynda didn't
come here just to sign things.

16:06.967 --> 16:09.034
Oh, of course, of course.
Sorry, I just, you know,

16:09.036 --> 16:11.403
I, I geeked out a bit.
(chuckles)

16:11.405 --> 16:13.305
Oh, that's okay.
You can't imagine how often

16:13.307 --> 16:16.108
I get roped into these kinds
of conversations.

16:16.110 --> 16:17.976
Roped? Or...

16:17.978 --> 16:19.645
...lassoed?

16:20.980 --> 16:24.116
Oh, God. He's gonna tie her up
and throw her in a van.

16:24.118 --> 16:27.653
No, no. This is an original
Wonder Woman Lasso of Truth.

16:27.655 --> 16:29.922
I-I got it at Comic Con '88.

16:29.924 --> 16:32.391
Yeah, back when only
the really cool people went.

16:34.327 --> 16:37.629
Whoever is wearing the lasso
must tell the truth.

16:37.631 --> 16:39.732
(giggles) Is this
the best night of my life?

16:39.734 --> 16:41.333
It is.

16:42.869 --> 16:45.170
Are you completely oblivious
to social cues?

16:45.172 --> 16:46.839
You are.

16:46.841 --> 16:49.374
Oh, oh, would you mind
posing with it

16:49.376 --> 16:50.943
so I can snap a quick picture?

16:51.945 --> 16:53.946
Alan. (whispers): Enough.
Mm-hmm?

16:53.948 --> 16:57.616
No. It, it's okay.
Let's just take the picture.

16:57.618 --> 17:00.385
Oh great, great. Oh,
crud. The memory's full.

17:00.387 --> 17:02.121
Uh, uh, let me just
delete a few.

17:02.123 --> 17:05.424
Good-bye, Jake.
Good-bye, Jake.

17:05.426 --> 17:07.793
Oh, kitty, hang in there.

17:07.795 --> 17:09.194
Good-bye, Jake.

17:09.196 --> 17:11.597
Okay, would you like to...
Yes!

17:14.434 --> 17:16.835
Hurry back.

17:16.837 --> 17:17.936
It's going well, isn't it?

17:17.938 --> 17:20.038
I have chimps smarter than you.

17:21.708 --> 17:24.243
I'm really sorry
about tonight.

17:24.245 --> 17:26.078
Oh, it's okay.
He's harmless.

17:26.080 --> 17:28.380
He &lt;i>is&lt;/i> harmless, right?

17:28.382 --> 17:31.650
Yeah, he's harmless,
clueless, homeless.

17:31.652 --> 17:32.985
He's pretty much "less."

17:32.987 --> 17:35.921
(laughs) Still,
I'm glad I came over.

17:35.923 --> 17:37.389
It's really good
to see you again.

17:37.391 --> 17:39.792
Yeah, it's good to see you, too.
And you look amazing.

17:39.794 --> 17:42.561
Or, should I say,
"wonder-ful."

17:42.563 --> 17:45.898
See? When you do it, it's cute.
(chuckles)

17:45.900 --> 17:47.733
Oh, uh, Jenny,

17:47.735 --> 17:48.801
this is Lynda Car...

17:48.803 --> 17:52.070
Lynda freakin' Carter.

17:52.072 --> 17:53.605
Nice to meet you.

17:53.607 --> 17:55.340
Jenny is
Alan's niece.

17:55.342 --> 17:57.843
Ah, well, I won't
hold that against you.

17:57.845 --> 18:00.813
Beautiful &lt;i>and&lt;/i> funny.

18:00.815 --> 18:02.080
(chuckles)
Aren't you sweet.

18:02.082 --> 18:04.716
Oh, I can be way sweeter.

18:04.718 --> 18:06.485
Or less, if that's
what you're into.

18:06.487 --> 18:08.086
Hmm.

18:08.088 --> 18:09.621
You still like
wearing cuffs?

18:09.623 --> 18:14.326
Okay. All right, uh, Jenny,
isn't your bedroom that way?

18:14.328 --> 18:17.095
(whispers):
What he said.

18:18.531 --> 18:22.601
See? I told you the
gays really like me.

18:22.603 --> 18:25.971
I'm sorry. I, I,
I actually, I do have to ask:

18:25.973 --> 18:28.340
does Alan have
a shot with you?

18:28.342 --> 18:29.975
&lt;i>That&lt;/i> Alan?

18:29.977 --> 18:32.945
You do know I'm Lynda
freakin' Carter, right?

18:32.947 --> 18:36.515
Okay. Asked
and answered.

18:36.517 --> 18:39.685
It seems that everyone
in this house wants to be with me

18:39.687 --> 18:41.687
except the one that I want.
(chuckles) Yeah.

18:41.689 --> 18:43.956
Wait, what?

18:44.591 --> 18:47.125
Okay, I made room for...

18:47.127 --> 18:49.194
Betrayal!

18:51.598 --> 18:53.832
♪

19:08.014 --> 19:10.182
Dude, seriously?

19:10.184 --> 19:12.351
No wonder you
brought her out here. Oh!

19:12.353 --> 19:16.121
God, I'm so angry I forgot to
emphasize the word "wonder."

19:16.123 --> 19:18.257
Alan, it's not what you think.
Oh, really?

19:18.259 --> 19:19.758
'Cause I'm thinking you're
kissing Lynda Carter.

19:19.760 --> 19:22.661
What is going on?
Oh, I'll tell you what's going on.

19:22.663 --> 19:25.197
Your son, my ex-friend,
still roommate,

19:25.199 --> 19:26.698
just double-crossed me.

19:26.700 --> 19:29.501
Alan, you're embarrassing yourself.
Oh, am I?

19:29.503 --> 19:31.036
Okay, I'm not
gonna do this.

19:31.038 --> 19:32.170
Oh, aren't you?

19:32.172 --> 19:33.605
Okay, that's it.

19:33.607 --> 19:34.940
(shrieks)
(Alan screams)

19:34.942 --> 19:36.708
Oh, this is about
to really suck.

19:36.710 --> 19:38.510
(thuds)

19:48.054 --> 19:49.822
Morning. (sighs)

19:49.824 --> 19:51.090
Morning.

19:51.092 --> 19:55.394
(clucks tongue) Listen, uh,
about last night...

19:55.396 --> 19:58.530
Let's just drop it.

19:58.532 --> 20:00.566
Fair enough.

20:07.607 --> 20:10.409
Again, I-I am
very sorry.

20:10.411 --> 20:12.778
I got it. Mo-Moving on.

20:16.082 --> 20:20.586
I know you would never
intentionally try to hurt me.

20:20.588 --> 20:22.554
We're past it.

20:22.556 --> 20:26.892
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>
